 "best_diff": "--- initial\n+++ best\n@@ -19,7 +19,32 @@\n     features (they are standardized and a bias is added), so nonlinear structure only\n     helps if a feature expresses it. Only the Python standard library may be used.\n \n-    Current method: the raw inputs.\n+    Features:\n+      f0 = x1 (raw)\n+      f1 = x2 (raw)\n+      f2 = x6 (raw)\n+      f3 = 10 ** (math.log(x3 + 1e-9) / 3.0)   # log-cubic of skewed positive x3 to handle lognormal tail\n+      f4 = x4**2 + x5**2                         # squared distance from origin for uniform inputs x4,x5\n+      f5 = x4 * x5                                # product interaction of uniforms (candidate XOR-like quadrant)\n+      f6 = x1 * x3                                 # raw cross term x1*x3\n+      f7 = x2 * x5                                 # raw cross term x2*x5\n+      f8 = 0.25 * math.log(x3 + 1e-9)            # scaled log of skewed x3 (mix with cubic)\n     \"\"\"\n-    return list(row)\n+    eps = 1e-9\n+    x1, x2, x3, x4, x5, x6 = row\n+    f0 = x1\n+    f1 = x2\n+    f2 = x6\n+    # log-cubic of positive skewed input: (log(x3))^p with p=3 then scaled by 10**(1/3) to moderate magnitude\n+    f3 = (math.log(x3 + eps)) ** 3.0 * 0.25   # note: previous used log-linear, now cubic log for heavier tail\n+    # radius-like circular features from uniform inputs\n+    f4 = x4**2 + x5**2\n+    # product interaction between x4 and x5 (already f5)\n+    f5 = x4 * x5\n+    # pairwise cross terms with raw inputs\n+    f6 = x1 * x3\n+    f7 = x2 * x5\n+    f8 = 0.25 * math.log(x3 + eps)   # scaled log feature\n+    out = [f0, f1, f2, f3, f4, x4, x5, f5, f6, f7, f8]\n+    return out\n # OMEGA-BLOCK-END\n",
